    "turn_text": "you look at the increased demand for energy over the course of the next decade or two, because of artificial intelligence and how much of an energy sucked at is to do those AI searches, it's like 10 to 20 times more energy than a traditional Google search. So that's why you're seeing all these data centers being built in Virginia and Ohio and other places. It's because of that. And then you look at the 800,000 manufacturing jobs, the reassuring that's happening around chips, EVs, batteries, et cetera. That's what's increasing the demand. So go into Pennsylvania and embrace natural gas. It has been displacing coal, which has been great for the environment. And we need affordable base load energy that wind and solar cannot provide right now. So go in and wrap your arms around it and talk about this is a high class problem because of manufacturing, because of us trying to dominate AI. And this is about national security and talk about it in that aspect. I think those two things, manufacturing in a kind of a pragmatic energy policy would move a lot of kind of independent voters, say, okay, she gets it. And let's get the work building the country and building the middle class.",
