    "turn_idx": 30,
    "turn_text": "There were some critiques in Politico this week, in fact, on this point. One that I saw said that just the vice president is a lot more comfortable talking about the care economy was the phrase that they use versus manufacturing industry, et cetera. I think that that is probably logical just given her background and the sort of issues in California versus perhaps the issues that are in the Midwest. What do you think are some of the things that she needs to understand in order to really make that connection that you're talking about? Because I agree, I don't think she's made it yet. And I don't think that she's walked people through it in terms of her shifts on some of these issues in a way that people necessarily find to be believable, that feels more like positioning than something that they can really have trust in.",
