  {
    "episode_id": 95568,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95568.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 31,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I mean we all in any job that we have you learn more and you understand more and politics is no different and I know that the standard is so high that you know you've got to be perfect and perfect on everything but I feel like she's really grown into the VP position and has a better understanding than she did when she was just California. But for me, I think her real passion has been her whole life as a prosecutor and AG and even as a senator is the issues of justice. But it's not a big step to talk about economic justice and economic fairness. And so I think it's right in her wheelhouse. I just think the message has got to get out. And you could see them building the campaign. So my hope is that this is the next iteration, the next play, the next chapter. It's about rallying the base, which she did. It's about she talked about housing, which is a huge issue, especially among young black men. who felt like nobody had a housing policy for them, even though they're out there scrapping and trying to work. So I think she's starting to build that out. I think even the comment of like, I own a gun and her telling Oprah yesterday that you come and you break into my house, you're going to get shot. I mean, like those are little cultural things are like, okay, now she's kind of talking my language. You know, I mean, I don't whatever your issue is on guns, she seems tough, right? No one's going to mess. Like she's layering this in. But I think, you know, we're down that we're down to 50 days less than 50 days. This manufacturing middle class economics has got to be, I think, front and center. and in the persuasion piece and especially in Pennsylvania and Michigan and Wisconsin, but those issues play everywhere. You know, that's an Arizona issue, that's a Georgia issue, that's a North Carolina issue too. So I think she's got to be the next chapter of this campaign.",
