  {
    "episode_id": 95568,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95568.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 32,
    "turn_text": "In your congressional career and obviously outside of it as well, you've been one of the people who's been upfront about the ways that China has screwed us over over the years in a host of different areas. In terms of the policy that we have toward China, how do you think that that ought to be something that is brought up to really emphasize the need to continue putting, being competitive with them, having the kind of reshoring that you mentioned, and having that be something that's key in terms of understanding the way that we view them going forward, as that's almost certainly going to be a major foreign policy issue that the next president is gonna have to deal with either way.",
