    "turn_text": "There's a great, there's a great documentary called Congressman from Crying Town that a friend of mine, Eric Murphy did on him. And if you want to have your mind blown about what was actually going on in Youngstown, Ohio, when he was coming up, it's absolutely incredible. He, he was a master of He was a super good politician. He just came up in a time when taking money and taking bribes is like all part of it. He didn't think he was doing anything wrong, honestly. But he always kept the kind of big issues front and center. And the one thing I did learn from him is that you got to have the guts to take on your own party when need be. He was not afraid to part ways with the Democrats if he felt like the Democrats were moving in the wrong direction. He would at least speak up about it. You know, maybe took a little too far here or there, but I learned that from him that if you're going to be in politics and you want people to respect you, people don't just respect you because you take on the opposition party. People will respect you even more if you have the guts to take on your own party, and that was a great lesson. He was the most charismatic guy I ever met in my life. I met Bill Clinton a million times. I met Barack Obama a million times. I met George W. Bush. He was the absolute most charismatic person I ever met in my life. I,",
